    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0449" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.21/929½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d457-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-23">December 23, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have your letter of December twenty-second in regard to Colombian affairs. I
                    think we should meet this proposal more than half way—the conversations to
                    proceed either here or down there, whichever they wish. They should include also
                    the possibility of exchange of information in relation to certain other
                    Nationals in the Republic of Colombia near the Panama border.</p>
                <closer><signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
